{/* KEY FACTS AT A GLANCE */}  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-8 px-6">
<div class="key-facts-box">
<span class="section-tag" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem">
At a Glance</span>
<ul class="key-facts-list">
<li>
<strong>
Location</strong>
Red Hill (Marpo Ri), central Lhasa, Tibet — 3,700m (12,139 ft) above sea level</li>
<li>
<strong>
Tickets</strong>
CNY 200 peak (May-Oct) / CNY 100 off-peak (Nov-Apr); students 50% off</li>
<li>
<strong>
Hours</strong>
9:30 AM – 3:30 PM daily; last entry at 3:30 PM sharp</li>
<li>
<strong>
Visitor cap</strong>
2,300 per day — reserve 5-7 days ahead in peak season</li>
<li>
<strong>
Foreign visitors</strong>
Tibet Travel Permit required — start the process 6-8 weeks before travel</li>
<li>
<strong>
Inside visit</strong>
2-3 hours; photography prohibited in chapels; dress code applies</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-10 px-6">
<div class="urgency-box">
<div class="urgency-icon">
<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="white" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round">
<circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
<polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/>
</svg>
</div>
<div class="urgency-body">
<p class="urgency-title">
Peak season is open -- book before tickets sell out</p>
<p class="urgency-desc">
May through October. Daily cap of just 2,300 visitors. During July-September, tickets routinely sell out 5-7 days in advance. <a href="/visit" class="urgency-link">
See booking guide &rarr;</a>
</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
    {/* PLANNING TIMELINE */}
